  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "This is an issue we've been experiencing in various RP instances.\nRegardless of if a given instance is at or under soft cap - or below hard cap -  random players will attempt to join an instance and then be sent off to a separate instance.\nIf we create a new instance, the issue no longer impacts those being afflicted with the issue above, but instead seemingly afflicts a random user attempting to enter the new instance.\nWhen the issue happens, those effected see this in their output logs:\n2021.09.22 22:36:03 Log        -  [Behaviour] Successfully joined room\n2021.09.22 22:36:03 Log        -  [Behaviour] Spent 0.08389282s entering world.\n2021.09.22 22:36:03 Log        -  [Behaviour] Waiting to enter network room\n2021.09.22 22:36:04 Log        -  [Behaviour] OnConnected\n2021.09.22 22:36:04 Log        -  [Behaviour] OnJoinRoomFailed\n2021.09.22 22:36:04 Log        -  [Behaviour] Resetting game flow because \"Failed to join room: \": [SkipLogin, TryAlternateInstance]\nAgain, this seems to happen regardless of a given instance's population size.",
